KNOWNBUG
fair_polarity1.btor2

^\[fair3\] : REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Same bug as justice_polarity1.btor2, for a BTOR2 `fair` node: a
fairness condition is a liveness violation pattern like `justice`, so
finding a path along which it holds infinitely often means the property
is VIOLATED. btor_ebmc_language.cpp instead lowers `fair` directly as
G(F(condition)) and checks it with the ordinary universal engine, so
the polarity is inverted. Here the condition is the constant 1, so a
fair witness trivially exists on every path, yet the tool reports
PROVED (as an outright tautology) instead of REFUTED.
